These are some problems I've faced whilst doing assignment 1
I've also listed the solutions and how I overcame it

Overall Game Play:
- Problem- At first I tried to do one big composable function for the game play, but then I started mixing the UI with too much logic
- Solution- I split it up into 3 categories: GamePlayState, GamePlayController, then the GamePlayScreen. So I made an entity, controller and a 'boundary' (Composable) object

Game Play State Object:
- Problem- I made an object of this inside the GamePlayScreen, so it was mutable, however, I noticed the composable only tracks the overall object not the contents within it
- Solution- I had to explicitly make the variables  "by mutableStateOf" or something similar because that notifies the composable if it actually changes

Changing Screens:
- Problem- I had multiple screen I had to change to, and it was getting harder to track to which screen appears or not
- Solution- I should've probably made a ScreenController class and then change it from there, BUT I just simply used a currentScreen variable within the compose and then a "when" to change screens
